                <pb facs="0612" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg532"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.35E1/146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-05-19T19:00:00-04:00">May 19, 1936—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>168. Reference Department’s instruction 1236 of May 11, 1936. In presenting a
                    copy of the memorandum you may state orally that the <pb facs="0613" n="533"
                        xml:id="pg533"/> Philippine Government has indicated that it will
                    participate in the proposed International Sugar Conference through
                    representation on the American Delegation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
